#RadioCtrl0 0    

AV_SW_MAX_DM 1200
TLAG_DM 0
A_SW_MAX_DM 720
*TPREV 0.6
*GAIN 0.7
VLOW_DRIVER 10
SET_PATH_WIDTH 0.1
SET_PATH_DASH_INTERVAL 0.5
SET_PATH_VERTEX_INTERVAL 0.25
SET_PATH_DZ 0.03
SET_PATH_COLOR 0 0 1

TPREV_CONSTANT 0.6

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This target lane change path is intended to be scaled based on the width of a lane (ltarg_gain is typically set to lane_ctr) to go from the left-hand lane center to the right-hand lane center.
#
#Also, the starting station SSTART_LTARG should be set via an event to be at or in front of the current station. The duration of the lane change (2) is intended to be scaled by vehicle speed (m/s), meaing that the maneuver will take 2 seconds if SSCALE_LTARG is set to VX.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Control: Steering by the Closed-loop Driver Model; { Lane Changes } Go to Right 1m, dS = 2m
